        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(process): trim UTF-8 boundary on win32 in truncated command output",
        "body": "## Problem\n\n`trimTruncatedUtf8Boundary` in `src/process/exec-output.ts` skipped UTF-8 boundary trimming entirely when `process.platform === \"win32\"`. On Windows, when command output exceeded `maxOutputBytes` and was truncated mid-codepoint, the partial UTF-8 bytes were left in the buffer. Downstream `Buffer.toString(\"utf8\")` then emitted U+FFFD replacement characters in truncated command output shown to users (doctor diagnostics, cron job output, plugin command output).\n\n## Fix\n\nRemove the `process.platform === \"win32\"` bypass from the early-return guard. The trimming logic (continuation-byte trimming in tail mode, `TextDecoder({ fatal: true })` probing in head mode) is platform-independent and works correctly on win32.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nA new test `real command output with UTF-8 emoji does not produce U+FFFD when truncated` runs an actual `node -e` command that outputs 10 emoji (40 bytes) and truncates via `maxOutputBytes: 18` (4.5 emoji). The `runCommandWithTimeout` flow exercises the full capture → `finalizeCapturedOutput` → `trimTruncatedUtf8Boundary` path on real command output:\n\n- **With fix:** Head mode keeps 4 full emoji (16 bytes), trimming the partial 5th → `stdout === \"😀😀😀😀\"`, no U+FFFD, `stdoutTruncatedBytes === 24`\n- **Without fix (win32 bypass):** The partial code point would remain → `stdout` would contain U+FFFD\n\n```\n ✓ |process| ../../src/process/exec.test.ts (42 tests | 1 skipped) 3237ms\n     ✓ real command output with UTF-8 emoji does not produce U+FFFD when truncated\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  41 passed | 1 skipped (42)\n```\n\nThe win32-specific behavior is covered by unit tests that mock `process.platform = \"win32\"` and verify trimming works in both head and tail modes (previously these would skip trimming entirely).\n\n## Risk\n\nMinimal. The fix only removes a platform bypass that prevented trimming on win32. All other platforms were already trimming correctly. The trimming logic is unchanged.",
